# DashBerry busybox config fragment, merged over buildroot's default
# busybox.config (BR2_PACKAGE_BUSYBOX_CONFIG_FRAGMENT_FILES).
#
# CONFIG_TC — Linux traffic control (`tc`). Disabled because it does not
# COMPILE any more, and because this card has no use for it.
#
# busybox 1.33.2's networking/tc.c reads TCA_CBQ_*, struct tc_cbq_lssopt,
# struct tc_cbq_wrropt, TCF_CBQ_LSS_BOUNDED and friends out of
# <linux/pkt_sched.h>. The CBQ queueing discipline was removed from Linux and
# its uapi definitions went with it, so on the rpi-6.16.y headers this image
# now builds against, every one of those identifiers is undeclared and the
# applet fails to compile. Nothing about that is fixable from here: the kernel
# does not implement CBQ any more, so an applet that configures it has nothing
# to talk to even if it did build.
#
# This is the first failure caused by the kernel repin rather than by host
# tooling — and it is the benign shape of it. `tc` shapes network traffic on a
# board whose only network interface is the USB gadget it streams video over.
# Upstream busybox reached the same conclusion independently and disables the
# applet by default in later releases.
#
# If a future busybox is picked up that builds tc against modern headers, this
# line can go; nothing else in the image depends on it being absent.
# CONFIG_TC is not set
